{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "id": "msg_011CfRwLhT7new5qzNQaC7Xz", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The Bash tool blocks standalone `sleep` commands to prevent wasteful delays. This is by design to keep the system efficient.\n\nIf you need to actually wait for 30 seconds, I have a couple of alternatives:\n\n1. **Run it in the background** \u2013 This starts the sleep without blocking, and you can continue with other work:\n   ```bash\n   sleep 30 &\n   ```\n\n2. **Use with `run_in_background: true`** \u2013 This runs the sleep and notifies you when it completes.\n\nWhich would you prefer,"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1130, "cache_read_input_tokens": 14744, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1130}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0b5459b3-a28c-42a4-ade3-5299f7bc10e1", "uuid": "41ebdb21-88c9-40b9-b33d-c5f58227fadc", "timestamp": "2026-09-26T11:02:20.260Z", "request_id": "req_011CfRwLgz61H99BRg19JirD", "aborted": true}
